# CHANGELOG.md accumulates one prepended entry per branch under the
# "## [Unreleased]" heading, so any two branches conflict on the same
# top-of-file hunk even though their entries are independent blocks. The
# built-in union merge driver resolves that hunk by keeping both sides'
# lines -- exactly what the manual resolution always is here -- and is the
# driver git's own documentation names for ChangeLog-style files. Caveat:
# union resolves silently, so a genuine same-line rewrite of an existing
# entry would surface as both versions side by side in review rather than
# as a conflict; for a changelog that is visible and low-stakes, for code
# it would not be, which is why only CHANGELOG.md gets the driver.
CHANGELOG.md merge=union
